## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CAPA from data governance, not just incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model for evidence, artifacts, and policy checks
- Lifecycle state machine with DETECT → INVESTIGATE → CONTAIN → REMEDIATE → VERIFY → CLOSED
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA creation/update with linked traces
- Region-aware compliance metrics (violation rate, MTTR, FP rate)
- RCA template and canary rollout with automated data redaction

## Code Example
```javascript
// CAPA data model sketch (TypeScript)
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  policyChecks: string[];
  region: string;
  state: 'DETECTED'|'INVESTIGATING'|'CONTAINED'|'REMEDIATED'|'VERIFIED'|'CLOSED';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you surface policy checks in runtime dashboards?
- How would you automate data redaction in canary tests before broader rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests designing a scalable CAPA program for multi-tenant real-time pipelines with cross-region controls and regulatory considerations, not just a checklist.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence lineage and PII flags
- Region- and tenant-aware state machine
- Minimal REST API for evidence-linked CAPAs
- Per-tenant metrics and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback for CDC changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model (Typescript)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  schemaVersion: string;
  eventId?: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  traces: string[];
  timestamp: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'contained'|'mitigated'|'verified'|'closed';
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement data lineage capture across CDC and streaming layers?
- What rollback safety checks would you add to the canary plan?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a robust, auditable CAPA for external data sources, focusing on provenance, containment speed, and reproducibility of fixes in a multi-source pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- External data provenance and signatures
- Drift detection and automated containment
- CAPA data model: evidence, lineage, owners
- Metrics for containment, recurrence, and verification
- RCA templates and canary rollback planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: verify feed signature before ingestion
function verifySignature(feedPayload, signature, key) {
  const h = crypto.createHmac('sha256', key);
  h.update(feedPayload);
  return h.digest('hex') === signature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle revocation of compromised feeds without delaying normal ingestion?
- What audits or reports would you expose to satisfy regulatory or governance needs?

